    "body": "## Overview\n\nApply EP weight filtering before InstantTensor I/O. Depends on scitix/InstantTensor#29 and its release; dependency pin pending.\n\n## Claims\n\nSkip non-local expert payloads while retaining scales, shared experts, and fused tensors. Unfiltered loading is unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nH100: `python -m pytest --noconftest -q tests/model_executor/model_loader/instanttensor_loader/test_weight_utils.py tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_ep_weight_filter.py` — 41 passed.\n\nTiny Qwen2MoE filtered-path smoke test: identical tokens and top-5 logprobs to safetensors for 2 prompts × 8 tokens, with all four experts selected on one GPU. Multi-GPU EP remains untested. Pre-commit checks and Linux-target mypy passed; macOS mypy hits two existing `posix_fadvise` errors.\n\n## Details\n\n11 production lines reuse the existing EP predicate. Filtered ranks load independently because NCCL loading requires identical layouts. #58016 covers the standard safetensors reader, rather than InstantTensor.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] Used `/pr-checklist`.\n- [x] Design fit.\n- [x] Testing and validation; multi-GPU limitation noted above.\n- [x] Code quality and style.\n- [x] Pull request contents.\n\n</details>\n",
    "changed_files": 3,
